null,"archived_by":null},{"id":410064485,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MTAwNjQ0ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/needs%20testing","name":"needs testing","color":"ffcc44","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-10-17T18:59:24Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T14:16:33Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS 24.04 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon 760M (radeonsi, phoenix, LLVM 20.1.2, DRM 3.57, 6.8.0-85-generic) - AMD Ryzen 5 7640U w/ Radeon 760M Graphics (12 threads) - 13.45 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf a node is freed too early (by using `Node.free()`), the project just stops running silently. No output, error or crash. It behaves as if it was intended to stop it. This is obviously wrong. (Looks like a silent crash to me but just speculating.)\nIf the node is freed with `Node.queue_free()` instead, the node is freed later and everything works as it is supposed to.\nI was using an `Area2D` but it's probably not exclusive to this node.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- make an `Area2D` with `VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D` as a child\n- move the area in any direction\n- connect the `screen_exited` signal to `free` (compared to `queue_free`)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nTechnically project independent but added one anyway.\n\n[issue-free-node.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22978163/issue-free-node.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://a